# Analyst — repository ignore rules.
#
# This file must exist BEFORE `git init`. Without it, a first `git add .`
# commits ~1.2 GB and, more seriously, `backend/data/analyst.db` — which holds
# every question asked, every answer, and every source DSN. Git history is
# forever; there is no cleanly removing that later.

# --- data: never committed -------------------------------------------------
# The SQLite store (answers, definitions, sources and their connection strings)
backend/data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Warehouses are never committed — not yours, and not ours.
#
# A sample warehouse used to live in the tree. It was a slice of a third-party
# public dataset with no licence we could establish, which made it unshippable,
# and it made "try the sample" the default path when "point it at your own data"
# is the product. It is now generated on demand by
# ./scripts/setup-sample-data.sh from CSVs in backend/internal/fixture/testdata,
# which ARE committed: they are ours, they are text, and a reviewer can read the
# numbers the conformance suite is scored against.
*.duckdb
sample/

# Local scratch from before the sample was generated: a ~1 GB third-party
# dataset and a Python venv. Neither is part of the project any more; these
# lines exist so a stale working copy cannot accidentally commit a gigabyte.
thelook/

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# --- Go --------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
dist/
# Compiled binaries dropped at package roots. `backend/probe` is 53 MB and was
# sitting in the tree; a stray binary is the classic accidental first commit.
backend/probe
backend/server
backend/cmd/server/server
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt

# --- Node / Next -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- internal working documents --------------------------------------------
# Kept locally, never published. The test for this section is simple: would a
# stranger reading it learn something about the PRODUCT, or about how we work
# and what we think of competitors?

# Readiness audits, plans, backlogs and the security review. These quote the
# author's absolute paths as evidence and describe findings in exploit detail;
# security-review.md in particular is a how-to until every fix has shipped.
# Their conclusions live in LICENSE, README, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY and
# ARCHITECTURE instead.
docs/oss/

# QA logs and their screenshots (2.2 MB). Dated internal sweeps — "BUG-04 ✅",
# "fix pass 2026-07-29" — that read as a work journal, not documentation.
docs/qa/

# A demo script whose numbers were measured against one specific database on
# one specific day. It goes stale silently, and a stale number in a trust
# product is worse than none.
docs/demo.md

# Competitive and strategic analysis: named competitor teardowns, market
# positioning, "where we can lead". Engineering conclusions from it already
# live in charting.md and data-viz.md, which ARE published. Same reasoning as
# product-research.md, which was moved out of the tree entirely.
docs/design/charting-roadmap.md

# The repository's previous README, kept when the product one was written. It
# still opens "# data-lab" and documents a venv/ layout — and it describes a
# dataset this project no longer uses at all (see NOTICE, "Bundled data").
docs/thelook-dataset.md

# --- tooling / logs --------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.playwright-mcp/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.claude/

# --- editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
